      "note": "Count prescribed oral NSAIDs, including those in combination products. Exclude low-dose antiplatelet aspirin. Check the route. Gels applied to the skin, eye drops, suppositories and injections do not count. For Voltaren, Indocid, Feldene and Toradol, check that the supplied form is oral. For aspirin, check the strength, directions and intended use. If these do not distinguish pain or inflammation from antiplatelet use, ask the pharmacist to confirm before counting it."
