  "rule_for_models": "Suspect a finding and cite each contributing supply when dates, quantities and directions support overlapping treatment with a prescribed oral NSAID, an ACE inhibitor or ARB and a diuretic, counting both groups when one product supplies the ACE inhibitor or ARB and the diuretic. If supplies of all three groups could plausibly overlap, including from a longer supply dispensed earlier, but unclear directions leave overlap uncertain, cite the supplies as a possible finding and ask the pharmacist to confirm the daily dose when used and whether the courses overlapped. Documented non-overlap gives no finding.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "Supply dates alone cannot show what the person took, medicines obtained elsewhere, non-prescription NSAIDs or the effect on kidney function.",
  "ask_the_gp": "Could you review the need for the oral NSAID during combined treatment and check the latest kidney function and potassium?",
  "urgency": "same_day",
  "draft": false,
